  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_004, multimodal/singleprofile/scvi_n200/imagenet_vit_l/weighted) achieves 0.5375 acc, only ~1.7% above RNA-only (config_023, 0.5203), while image-only is far weaker (0.2266). This suggests the image modality contributes modestly and the fusion mechanism may be a critical determinant of whether that contribution is realized. Question: config_002 is identical to config_004 except fusion changes from 'weighted' to 'concat', making it a clean single-variable A/B test that isolates the effect of fusion strategy. Why this is the best next experiment: Fusion is the most fundamental design decision in any multimodal model—it governs how the two modalities interact. Understanding whether weighted vs. concat matters will inform every subsequent multimodal experiment (profile setting, encoder choice, aggregation). Because the multimodal gain over RNA-only is small, knowing whether a different fusion could widen or eliminate that gap is essential before investing in more complex configurations (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, etc.). This minimal-change comparison maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
